  "result": "Excellent! All 257 tests pass (233 previous + 24 new credit note tests). Here's what was implemented:\n\n**src/errors.js**\n- Added `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH`: \"Credit note amount exceeds the invoice total.\"\n\n**src/credits.js**\n- `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, date)` helper that:\n  - Generates CN-YYYY-NNNN format (separate from invoice numbers)\n  - Filters only CN-prefixed numbers from existing list\n  - Maintains separate year-based counter from invoices\n  - Restarts counter annually\n  - Returns zero-padded 4-digit counter\n\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` that:\n  - Validates invoice status is 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (NOT_ISSUED if draft)\n  - Validates amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID if not)\n  - Validates amount \u2264 invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH if exceeded)\n  - Generates credit note with:\n    - number: CN-YYYY-NNNN (separate counter)\n    - invoiceNumber: reference to original invoice\n    - customerId: from invoice\n    - amount, reason, date: as provided\n  - Returns ok(creditNote)\n\n**Tests (24 total)**\n- Number generation and formatting (CN-2025-0001, etc.)\n- Separate CN counter from invoices (both can coexist in existingNumbers)\n- Year-based counter restart\n- Status validation (issued/partially_paid/paid accepted, draft rejected)\n- Amount validation (positive integer only)\n- Credit limits (amount \u2264 invoice total, full refunds allowed)\n- Integration with complex invoices (discounts, VAT, vouchers, payments)\n- Edge cases (empty list, unordered counters, padding)\n\nThe credit note system supports refund workflows while maintaining separate numbering sequences and proper audit trails.\n\nAll 257 tests pass (233 previous + 24 new).",
